* 332 Standard Internet Data Center \(IDC\) environment;
  * 333 At least one standard 19-inch rack with a top-of-rack \(TOR\) switch and five servers;
  * 334 Highly available cloud platform software;
  * 335 Highly available network topology;
  * 336 Highly available storage system in the form of traditional storage area network \(SAN\), software-defined storage 337 \(SDS\), or combination of the two.
  * 338 In Scenario C \(and its variants C.1/C.2\), a regional cloud will also host the O-CU functions.

* T-GM A and T-GM B clocks with performance class ITU-T G.8272 PRTC/T-GM type PRTC-B serving as grandmasters for O-DUs as well as O-RUs \(O-DUs require PRTC-A or better while O-RUs require PRTC-B\)
  * The Fronthaul Leafs acting as T-BCs in both the O-RU and O-DU synchronization path, with support for a minimum performance class ITU-T G.8273.2 T-BC Class B \(Class C is recommended\);
  * The Spine and O-Cloud Leaf switches acting as T-BCs in the O-DU synchronization path only, with the least demanding T-BC performance class ITU-T G.8273.2 T-BC Class A or better;
  * T-TSC implementation on the O-Cloud nodes with the least demanding performance class ITU-T G.8273.2, Annex C, T-TSC Class A or better.
